      "text": [
        {
          "id": "editorial",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "THE WHOLE HOLDS · WITHOUT FUSION",
          "title": "Three presences, one whole",
          "italic": "parā holds paśyantī, madhyamā, vaikharī",
          "body": "The registers are held within Symbolon as distinct offices of one descent of speech: Matheme the operative logic, Mytheme the formed image, Episteme the inspected utterance. Held — not collapsed into one another, and not set beside the whole as a fourth sibling. The slash stays active between them: distinction remains the form of belonging.\nEvery depth retains its point of departure and its route of return: what opens into a register can come back to the exact relation from which it opened. Four reading movements cross the whole — linear, radial, transverse, toroidal.\nSource of record: submission-package/essay/symbolon/README.md @ dbf3b17",
